Pins a parser gap, not a regression: inside a `name =` flow-decl chain,
a `|> if(cond)` step does not collect `| then` / `| else` arms on the
following lines — they surface as KORU010 stray continuations. The same
attachment works at a bare flow head (241) and inside `!` arm bodies
(210_314); the hole is if-specific arm collection on `|>` steps in
`=` bodies. Fix lives in src/parser.zig continuation collection.
